  "hypothesis": "Declared filecodes, placeholder suffixes, numbered stems and level aliases may form missing, duplicated or inconsistent static filenames or references.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Restrict expansions to the names and counts declared at the pinned sources; distinguish lexical consistency from runtime interpretation.",
  "observedBehavior": "13 role filecodes agree. All 39 placeholder joins and 65 authored quest-family filenames are accounted for. The tower stem has exactly three declared numbered levels/files. All 26 aliases resolve to declared prototypes and C topology fields. No unexplained static discrepancy.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "source",
    "scope": "Supplemental lexical joins and alias reference checks; original static v1 evidence unchanged.",
    "limitations": [
      "Quest joins are lexical consistency checks using the declared filecode and x-* suffixes, not execution of substitution logic.",
      "tower1/2/3 agree with declared base=3 and listed levels; no assertion about runtime stem selection or generated depth.",
      "Rog-fila/Rog-filb share an identifier; body equivalence remains untested.",
      "rogue/dummy lack literal assets; runtime marker behavior and Val-strt wrapper semantics remain excluded.",
      "No Lua, game handlers, level generation, special-level APIs, or C oracle executed.",
      "Role fields other than filecode and runtime marker/wrapper behavior are outside scope."
    ]
